   "P1",
   "Title: Zassenhaus Lemma/Lemma 1"
  ],
  [
   "P2",
   "Let $G$ be a [[Definition:Group|group]] whose [[Definition:Identity Element|identity]] is $e$."
  ],
  [
   "P3",
   "Let $H_1, H_2$ be [[Definition:Subgroup|subgroups]] of $G$."
  ],
  [
   "P4",
   "Let:"
  ],
  [
   "P5",
   "{{begin-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   "P6",
   "{{eqn | l = N_1"
  ],
  [
   "P7",
   "      | o = \\lhd"
  ],
  [
   "P8",
   "      | r = H_1"
  ],
  [
   "P9",
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   "P10",
   "{{eqn | l = N_2"
  ],
  [
   "P11",
   "      | o = \\lhd"
  ],
  [
   "P12",
   "      | r = H_2"
  ],
  [
   "P13",
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   "P14",
   "{{end-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   "P15",
   "where $\\lhd$ denotes the relation of being a [[Definition:Normal Subgroup|normal subgroup]]."
  ],
  [
   "P16",
   "Then:"
  ],
  [
   "P17",
   ":$N_1 \\paren {H_1 \\cap N_2} \\lhd N_1 \\paren {H_1 \\cap H_2}$"
  ],
  [
   1,
   "Consider arbitrary $x_n \\in N_1, x_h \\in H_1 \\cap H_2$."
  ],
  [
   2,
   ""
  ],
  [
   3,
   "Thus:"
  ],
  [
   4,
   ":$x_n x_h \\in N_1 \\paren {H_1 \\cap H_2}$"
  ],
  [
   5,
   ""
  ],
  [
   6,
   "Note that as $x_h \\in H_1 \\cap H_2$ it follows that $x_h \\in H_1$."
  ],
  [
   7,
   ""
  ],
  [
   8,
   "We aim to show that:"
  ],
  [
   9,
   ":$x_n x_h N_1 \\paren {H_1 \\cap N_2} \\paren {x_n x_h}^{-1} \\subseteq N_1 \\paren {H_1 \\cap H_2}$"
  ],
  [
   10,
   ""
  ],
  [
   11,
   "thus demonstrating $N_1 \\paren {H_1 \\cap N_2} \\lhd N_1 \\paren {H_1 \\cap H_2}$ by the [[Normal Subgroup Test]]."
  ],
  [
   12,
   ""
  ],
  [
   13,
   "We have:"
  ],
  [
   14,
   ""
  ],
  [
   15,
   "{{begin-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
